Hi *,

using build profiles breaks debian-ports architectures, all of them:

http://buildd.debian-ports.org/status/package.php?p=3Dx264

=E2=94=82Dependency installability problem for [33]x264 on alpha, hppa, m68=
k, sh4, sparc64 and x32:
=E2=94=82
=E2=94=82x264 build-depends on missing:
=E2=94=82- empty-dependency-after-parsing

wdiff shows:

Version: =E2=8C=A62:0.146.2538+git121396c-2=E2=8C=AB =E2=96=B62:0.146.2538+=
git121396c-3=E2=97=80

Build-Depends: [=E2=80=A6] libgpac-dev (>=3D =E2=8C=A60.5.0+svn4288~),=E2=
=8C=AB =E2=96=B60.5.0+svn4288~) <!stage1>,=E2=97=80 [=E2=80=A6]

So this means that because someone added the build profiles thing,
wanna-build (or something else in the component stack) on dpo can
no longer calculate B-D installability for those packages, which
sorta defeats the purpose of adding it.

bye,
//mirabilos
